This confirms it: the master branch (first parent, containing `f6e9e9d4d`) and the `dev_UniTime43` branch (second parent, containing `c11786987`) each independently introduced the identical `getSession()` method (same author, same commit message, same diff, just diverged before merge). Both are true ancestors of HEAD and both introduced the same bug.

## Bug-Introducing Commits
BIC: f6e9e9d4db7a0992ab7e58f46298e65060440b00, c11786987649f39b0fd655acc5886f270d0e2f13

## Reasoning

**(1) Investigation:** I traced the history of `JavaSource/org/unitime/timetable/model/CourseEvent.java` with `git log --follow -p` to find when `getSession()` was introduced. The fix commit (522101e32) adds a `null` check before iterating `getRelatedCourses()`. I found `getSession()` was first added by commit `c11786987`. However, `git log --all` (without `--follow`) showed a different commit, `f6e9e9d4d`, with the exact same diff and message. Checking `git merge-base --is-ancestor`, both commits are true ancestors of HEAD, and neither is an ancestor of the other — they sit on two divergent lines of history.

**(2) The change:** Both commits add:
```java
public Session getSession() {
	for (RelatedCourseInfo rc: getRelatedCourses())
		return rc.getCourse().getInstructionalOffering().getSession();
	return null;
}
```
without guarding against `getRelatedCourses()` returning `null`. This is exactly the defect that the bug-fix commit patches by adding `if (getRelatedCourses() == null) return null;`.

**(3) Supporting evidence:** The merge commit `73698fd3f "Moving dev_UniTime43 to master"` has two parents: the master line (containing `f6e9e9d4d`, dated 2018-07-15 09:39) and the `dev_UniTime43` line (containing `c11786987`, dated 2018-07-15 12:29). Both commits are titled "Event Detail: Enrollments Export CSV" by the same author and contain byte-identical diffs to `CourseEvent.java` — i.e., the same change was made independently/duplicated on both branches before they were merged into the final history. Since both are ancestors of HEAD and both introduce the unguarded `getSession()` method, both are bug-introducing commits (they represent the same logical change appearing twice in the reconstructed linear-ish history due to the branch merge).

**Uncertainty:** I'm confident the buggy code (missing null check in `getSession()`) originates from this single logical change; the only uncertainty is attributing it to one or both hashes due to the branch-merge duplication artifact in this repository's history. I'm listing both since both are genuine ancestors introducing identical bugged code.

